  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "A new name in the first ten",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Son & Mark & Ronen climbed from 20th at the midnight baseline to seventh on the observed ARC-AGI-3 board, lifting their public score from 35.45 to 39.24. The team now sits just behind the last dance and NVARC3. That is the sharpest change near the leaders overnight; it does not settle where the team will stand after other submissions finish evaluating."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The leader still sets the mark",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-roster-1",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-roster-0",
        "person-dries-smit-roster-1",
        "person-dries-smit-roster-0"
      ],
      "text": "Yi-Chia Chen remains first at 62.96, ahead of Tufa Labs at 56.52. Chen’s verified Kaggle account is threerabbits, listed on this ARC-AGI-3 team and a separate ARC-AGI-2 entry. Tufa has a roster in both contests too, but the two leaderboards measure different races."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The chase has layers",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-roster-1",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-roster-0",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-archive-0",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-archive-0"
      ],
      "text": "Behind Tufa, mtg stands third at 45, Majkel1337 fourth at 42.66 and NVARC3 fifth at 40.97. The last dance holds sixth at 39.30, only a narrow step above the overnight climber. NVARC3’s observed roster includes Jean-François Puget and Ivan Sorokin, the credited members of the 2025 champion NVARC; the 2026 entry has its own team ID and current result."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Movement farther down",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "mikelou1 rose from 111th at the baseline to 24th with a score of 35.42. Lord Han Solo improved its score to 36.98 and stands 16th, while Nick2187 reached 21st. Those gains show how quickly places can change below the front group; the public medal positions remain provisional."
    }
